{{ $json.status === 'completed' ? 'Your transfer has been completed successfully.' : ($json.status === 'pending_additional_signatures' ? 'Your transfer request has been recorded, but this account requires every holder to approve transfers before funds move.' : 'Your transfer could not be completed.') }}

Amount: {{ ($('Resolve Transfer Target & Authorize').item.json.amount / 100).toFixed(2) }} {{ $('Resolve Transfer Target & Authorize').item.json.source_currency }}
From: {{ $('Resolve Transfer Target & Authorize').item.json.source_account_number }}
To: {{ $('Resolve Transfer Target & Authorize').item.json.destination_lookup }}
{{ $json.status === 'completed' ? 'Transaction ID: ' + $json.transaction_id : ($json.status === 'pending_additional_signatures' ? 'Approvals received: ' + $json.consents_count + ' of ' + $json.required + ' required. The other holder(s) have been notified.' : 'Reason: ' + ($json.error || 'Transfer rejected by banking rules')) }}

{{ $json.status === 'completed' ? 'Thank you for banking with us.' : 'No funds have been moved from your account yet.' }}

Digital Bank Transfer Service

parameters.jsCode:
const ctx = $('Classify Intent & Authorize Request').item.json;
const td = ctx.transferDetails || {};
const authorized = ctx.authorizedAccounts || [];

const source = authorized.find(a => a.account_id === td.source_account_id && a.status === 'active');

if (!source) {
  return [{ json: {
    ok: false,
    reason: 'You do not have an active account authorized for outgoing transfers.',
    fromEmail: ctx.fromEmail, subject: ctx.subject, full_name: ctx.full_name
  } }];
}

if (source.holder_type === 'minor') {
  return [{ json: {
    ok: false,
    reason: 'This account is a minor account with view-only access. A guardian must initiate transfers on your behalf.',
    fromEmail: ctx.fromEmail, subject: ctx.subject, full_name: ctx.full_name
  } }];
}

if (!td.destination_account) {
  return [{ json: {
    ok: false,
    reason: 'We could not identify who to send it to. Name the destination either way: an account number ("send 5000 to ACC-1234567890") or their registered email address ("send 5000 to someone@example.com").',
    fromEmail: ctx.fromEmail, subject: ctx.subject, full_name: ctx.full_name
  } }];
}

if (!td.amount || td.amount <= 0) {
  return [{ json: {
    ok: false,
    reason: 'We could not identify a valid transfer amount. Please state the amount clearly.',
    fromEmail: ctx.fromEmail, subject: ctx.subject, full_name: ctx.full_name
  } }];
}

return [{ json: {
  ok: true,
  source_account_id: source.account_id,
  source_account_number: source.account_number,
  source_currency: source.currency,
  destination_lookup: td.destination_account,
  amount: td.amount,
  idempotency_key: td.idempotency_key,
  initiated_by_profile_id: ctx.profile_id,
  fromEmail: ctx.fromEmail, subject: ctx.subject, full_name: ctx.full_name
} }];

parameters.message:
=Hello {{ $('Resolve Transfer Target & Authorize').item.json.full_name }},

We could not send your transfer.

{{ (function(){
  const r = $json.reason;
  const looked = $('Resolve Transfer Target & Authorize').item.json.destination_lookup;
  if (r === 'ambiguous_recipient') return 'That person holds more than one account with us (' + ($json.candidates || []).join(', ') + '), so we cannot tell which one you meant. Please reply with the account number.';
  if (r === 'no_such_recipient') return 'We have no active account registered to ' + looked + '.';
  if (r === 'staff_address') return 'That address belongs to the bank, not to a customer account.';
  return 'We could not find the destination account you specified: ' + looked;
})() }}

You can name the destination either way: an account number ("send 5000 to ACC-1234567890") or the recipient's registered email address ("send 5000 to someone@example.com").

No funds have been moved from your account.

Digital Bank Transfer Service

=Hello {{ $('Resolve Dispute Request').item.json.full_name }},

We have opened a formal dispute and a specialist will investigate it personally.

Your dispute reference: {{ $json.ref_code }}
Account: {{ $json.account_number }}
{{ $json.disputed_amount ? 'Amount: Rs ' + ($json.disputed_amount / 100).toFixed(2) : 'You did not identify a specific transaction. If you can find the transaction reference on your statement, reply with it and we will attach it to this dispute.' }}

{{ $json.is_joint_account ? 'Because this is a joint account, we have also asked the other ' + ($json.holder_count - 1) + ' holder(s) for their side. You did not need their permission to raise this - but we do not decide it on one account holder-s word alone either.' : '' }}

WHAT HAPPENS NOW
A specialist reviews the dispute and everything we have. There is no automated decision here - a person decides. If the dispute is upheld and we can identify the transaction, we reverse it and recover the money.

We will email you the outcome. If anything else comes to mind in the meantime, just reply to this email.

Digital Bank Disputes Team

